RequestingDevice_HParam.description:
Requesting Software described in an object based on a FHIR 'Device' resource (Standard Base64 encoded JSON).
Access-control requirements for these headers depend on the receiving implementation. 

The identifier used, though arbitrary, should be consistent across instances of a product, the name and version of the product should also be accurate and consistent.

**Example object before encoding**
```json
{
  "resourceType": "Device",
  "identifier": [
    {
      "system": "https://consumersupplier.com/Id/device-identifier",
      "value": "SUPP-APP-1"
    }
  ],
  "deviceName": {
    "name": "Supplier product name",
    "type": "manufacturer-name"
  },
  "version": {
    "value": "1.0.0"
  }
}


This header describes the calling software; patient identity is established through the authenticated access-token context.

RequestingOrganisation_HParam.description:
Requesting Organization described in an object based on a FHIR 'Organization' resource (Standard Base64 encoded JSON).
This header is optional in the API definition because its use depends on the authentication mode. It MUST be provided for application-based authentication and SHOULD NOT be provided for patient-based authentication. It does not identify the patient and must not be used to establish patient authorisation.
In the example given an ODS code and the Organisation name is provided. Other identifiers are permitted if required. 

**Example object before encoding** 
  ```json
  {
    "resourceType": "Organization",
    "identifier": [
      {
        "value": "A1001",
        "system": "https://fhir.nhs.uk/Id/ods-organization-code"
      }
    ],
    "name": "My service provider name"
  }

  ```

RequestingPractitioner_HParam.description:
Requesting Practitioner described in an object based on a FHIR 'PractitionerRole' resource (Standard Base64 encoded JSON).

This item is not mandatory, however if the information is available it must be included in the request. Only in the event that it is not available, should it be omitted.

The example given shows a General Practitioner and their SDS Role profile Id.


**Example object before encoding** 
```json
{
  "resourceType": "PractitionerRole",
  "identifier": [
    {
      "system": "https://fhir.nhs.uk/Id/sds-role-profile-id",
      "value": "100334993514"
    }
  ],
  "code": [
    {
      "coding": [
        {
          "system": "http://snomed.info/sct",
          "code": "62247001",
          "display": "General practitioner"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}


Omit for a patient acting on their own behalf. This header does not confer practitioner privileges or patient access.
